[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability in this code relates to a Regular Expression Denial of Service (ReDoS) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises when the application allows user-supplied regex patterns to be processed without adequate validation or restrictions. If an attacker submits a specially crafted regex pattern that causes excessive backtracking, it can lead to significant performance degradation or even application crashes, as the regex engine may take an inordinate amount of time to evaluate the pattern against the file contents. This can result in a denial of service, where legitimate users are unable to access the service due to the resource exhaustion caused by the malicious regex input.

